WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.720
I don't want to talk a lot about this, but
I think it makes sense to say something about

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.720
it.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.170
A few days ago, Donald Trump and people around
him have switched to calling the Corona virus

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.370
the Chinese virus.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.250
And there was an immediate reaction from a
lot of people that's racist.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.630
It's xenophobic.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:18.869
So on and so forth.

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:23.909
And it may well be, but I want to give you
my take on where I am on this.

00:00:23.909 --> 00:00:29.939
This cannot be allowed to become a distraction
from the failed slow response from the Trump

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:33.880
administration and actually dealing with the
virus.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:40.100
I don't even care to argue about is Chinese
virus racist or isn't it?

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.670
Well, they call it the Spanish flu.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.489
Well, but the Spanish flu is really from Kansas
and or France.

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:48.300
It wasn't actually from Spain.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.910
That's a fine debate to have.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.210
I guess maybe.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.789
But if we allow there's a limited amount of
time in the day, there's a limited amount

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.750
of time that people are paying attention to
the news.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.290
There's a limited amount of time that people
put effort and time into answering the question,

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:11.200
what do I need to do right now to help rather
than hurt with coronavirus if we allow Trump

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.900
to make the discussion about Chinese virus?

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:17.000
We are taking time away from the important
stuff.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.740
He gets to control the narrative and in fact,
during yesterday's coronavirus briefing press

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:25.130
conference, that complete propaganda network.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.130
Okay.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.640
And one American use network that now has
a seat in the White House press briefing room.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.149
This journalist in the back asked some bizarre
question about is Chinese virus really racist?

00:01:36.149 --> 00:01:37.149
If it is, then.

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:41.630
Then the term Chinese food would also be racist
and Trump like the question and so on and

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:46.280
so forth, and was able to waste five minutes
talking about how unfairly The New York Times

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.290
treats him and CNN and all of this other stuff.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.450
Just don't allow it.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.500
It's idiotic.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.259
This Chinese virus stuff is completely idiotic.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:59.700
But the more we take the bait on it, the more
the attention is not on.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.180
Why aren't we testing?

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.780
Why aren't we taste testing large asymptomatic
populations to figure out how many people

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:11.110
who have no symptoms are potentially super
spreaders of the disease, et cetera, et cetera,

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.110
et cetera.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.290
So I don't even want to spend a lot of time
here.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:16.720
I think, you know, a couple of minutes I just
spent is enough.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.760
The Chinese virus stuff is crazy.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.930
But the more we feed into it and talk about
it, the less we're talking about the more

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:23.930
important stuff.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.250
So we're going to try to stay away from that
topic.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.819
We've got a full program for you today.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:31.819
Make sure you're following me on Twitter at
D Packman.

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:32.480
Much more coming right up.

